      "problem": "Simplify the product $(x - 3)(x^2 - 2x + 6).$",
      "worked_solution": "We distribute both terms of the binomial to the trinomial in the second parenthesis. Then, we simplify.\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t(x - 3)(x^2 - 2x + 6) &= \\\n\t\tx(x^2 - 2x + 6) - 3(x^2 - 2x + 6) &= \\\n\t\tx^3 - 2x^2 + 6x - 3x^2 + 6x - 18 &= \\\n\t\tx^3 - 5x^2 + 12x - 18\n\t}\n$$",
